    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d259">

                <pb facs="0529" n="395" sameAs="frus:frus1888p1/pg395"/>

                <head>No. 259.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Bayard to Mr. Chang Yen
                        Hoon.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1888-04-11"><hi rendition="#italic">April</hi> 11,
                        1888</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to transmit herewith for
                    your information in connection with my note to you of February 23, 1888,
                    relative to the murder of certain Chinese subjects on Snake River, Oregon, a
                    copy of a letter from the governor of the Territory of Idaho, dated the 3d
                    instant, upon the subject. It will be observed that, despite the excellent
                    disposition of Governor Stevenson, the very limited knowledge of the facts so
                    far as disclosed makes investigation difficult, if indeed it does not tend to
                    defeat the ends of justice.</p>
                <p>Accept, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">T. F.
                        Bayard.</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d259-a1.xml" xpointer="d259-a1"/>
            </div>
